# Redis appendonly directory, created in the working directory by
# packages/envelope-cache-redis/src/redis-cache.test.ts. That test turns
# `appendonly` ON deliberately, to prove `RedisEnvelopeCache.verify()` REFUSES a
# server whose configuration would let ciphertext reach disk, and turns it back
# off afterwards — Redis creates the directory in the moment in between. It
# holds a zero-length temp file and no data. The proof is worth the artefact.
appendonlydir/
verification-runs/
